WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:18.502
The next morning the travelers passed through the forest and came to a steep hill.

2
00:00:18.503 --> 00:00:24.643
"That will be a difficult climb," said the Scarecrow. "But over it we must go."

3
00:00:24.643 --> 00:00:29.980
He had started up the hill when a rough voice said, "Keep back!"

4
00:00:29.981 --> 00:00:33.448
"Who are you?" asked the Scarecrow.

5
00:00:33.449 --> 00:00:38.743
"This hill belongs to us. You cannot cross it," said the voice again.

6
00:00:38.744 --> 00:00:42.293
"But we must cross it," said the Scarecrow.

7
00:00:42.294 --> 00:00:46.412
"You will not!" said a flat-headed, armless creature.

8
00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:52.192
The Scarecrow did not fear such a helpless creature so he continued up the hill.

9
00:00:52.193 --> 00:01:00.561
The creature's head struck the Scarecrow like a hammer, and the Scarecrow went tumbling down the hill.

10
00:01:00.562 --> 00:01:06.475
The Hammer-Head called down, "Climbing the hill won't be as easy as you think."

11
00:01:06.476 --> 00:01:12.545
As Dorothy helped the Scarecrow up, the Tin Man suggested, "Let's call the Winged Monkeys.

12
00:01:12.546 --> 00:01:15.040
You can command them once more."

13
00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:18.002
Everyone thought it was an excellent idea.

14
00:01:18.003 --> 00:01:26.306
Dorothy put on the golden hat, spread her arms, and said, "By my command."

15
00:01:26.307 --> 00:01:31.932
A moment later the King landed, bowed, and said, "What do you command?"

16
00:01:31.933 --> 00:01:37.090
"Take us to the castle of Glinda, the Good Witch of the South," she answered.

17
00:01:37.091 --> 00:01:40.936
"It shall be done," answered the King.

18
00:01:40.937 --> 00:01:47.810
He and his Monkeys picked up the travelers and flew them south.

19
00:01:47.811 --> 00:01:53.597
The King and his followers dropped Dorothy and her friends off in front of Glinda's castle.

20
00:01:53.598 --> 00:01:58.823
Before the gate were three beautiful girls dressed in red.

21
00:01:58.824 --> 00:02:05.162
As Dorothy approached, one of the girls asked, "Why have you come to Glinda's castle?"

22
00:02:05.163 --> 00:02:08.462
"To see the Good Witch," answered Dorothy.

23
00:02:08.463 --> 00:02:13.884
"What is your name? I will find out if she will see you," said the girl.

24
00:02:13.885 --> 00:02:17.535
Dorothy and her friends gave their names, and soon they were admitted.

25
00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:23.370
They were taken to a room in which a beautiful woman sat upon a ruby throne.

26
00:02:23.371 --> 00:02:27.554
"What can I do for you, my child?" asked Glinda.

27
00:02:27.555 --> 00:02:32.629
"My greatest wish is to return to Kansas," answered Dorothy.

28
00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:38.604
"I can tell you how," said Glinda. "But I will need the golden hat."

29
00:02:38.605 --> 00:02:41.850
"You can have it," said Dorothy gladly.

30
00:02:41.851 --> 00:02:46.453
"Thank you," said Glinda, taking the hat from Dorothy.

31
00:02:46.454 --> 00:02:50.406
"I think I will need its three commands."

32
00:02:50.407 --> 00:02:55.962
"What will you do when Dorothy leaves?" Glinda asked the Scarecrow.

33
00:02:55.963 --> 00:03:00.109
"I will return to the Emerald City," answered the Scarecrow.

34
00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:02.766
"I can help," said Glinda.

35
00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:07.764
"My first command to the Winged Monkeys will be for them to bring you there."

36
00:03:07.765 --> 00:03:11.298
"Thank you," said the Scarecrow.

37
00:03:11.299 --> 00:03:16.721
"What will you do when Dorothy leaves?" Glinda asked the Tin Man.

38
00:03:16.722 --> 00:03:20.031
"I think the Winkies need me," said the Tin Man.

39
00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:22.891
"I would like to return to the Land of the West."

40
00:03:22.892 --> 00:03:29.409
"My second command to the Winged Monkeys will be for them to take you there," said Glinda.

41
00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:32.704
"Thank you," said the Tin Man.

42
00:03:32.705 --> 00:03:38.050
"What will you do when Dorothy leaves?" Glinda asked the Lion.

43
00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:44.158
"I will return to the forest where the animals have made me their king," answered the Lion.

44
00:03:44.159 --> 00:03:51.459
"My third command to the Winged Monkeys will be for them to take you there," said Glinda.

45
00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.835
"Thank you," said the Lion.

46
00:03:54.836 --> 00:04:00.282
"To the King of the Monkeys, I will give the golden hat," said Glinda.

47
00:04:00.283 --> 00:04:02.863
"He has earned his freedom."

48
00:04:02.864 --> 00:04:07.479
"Thank you for your kindness and for helping my friends," said Dorothy.

49
00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.180
"But how will I get to Kansas?"

50
00:04:10.181 --> 00:04:14.282
"Your silver shoes will take you there," said Glinda.

51
00:04:14.283 --> 00:04:20.995
"Just click the heels three times and tell the shoes where you want to go."

52
00:04:20.996 --> 00:04:26.986
Dorothy turned to the Good Witch and said, "Thank you for helping me and my friends return home."

53
00:04:26.987 --> 00:04:30.855
The Good Witch smiled as Dorothy hugged each of her friends.

54
00:04:30.856 --> 00:04:37.094
Then Dorothy held Toto in her arms and clicked the heels of her shoes three times.

55
00:04:37.095 --> 00:04:42.400
"I want to go home," she said.

56
00:04:42.401 --> 00:04:45.022
Suddenly everything began to spin.

57
00:04:45.023 --> 00:04:50.307
When Dorothy opened her eyes, she saw Aunt Em sitting next to her.

58
00:04:50.308 --> 00:04:53.229
"You're back," said Aunt Em.

59
00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:57.350
"Yes, it took me so long," said Dorothy.

60
00:04:57.351 --> 00:04:59.887
"I didn't know what the shoes could do."

61
00:04:59.888 --> 00:05:02.964
"Shoes?" asked Aunt Em.

62
00:05:02.965 --> 00:05:08.446
"Yes, the silver shoes from the Witch," answered Dorothy.

63
00:05:08.447 --> 00:05:14.180
"There's no witch," said Aunt Em. "But the cyclone nearly killed you.

64
00:05:14.181 --> 00:05:16.839
You are a very lucky girl."

65
00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:20.179
"But it wasn't a dream!" shouted Dorothy.

66
00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:30.691
"Dream or no dream," said Aunt Em. "I'm glad you're back."

67
00:05:30.692 --> 00:06:32.244
[caption_out@
